&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Silicon Valley, California, Archer is a leader in the next-gen aerospace sector building an end-to-end advanced air mobility platform that delivers air taxis, unmanned aircraft systems (“UAS”), aviation-related physical artificial intelligence (“AI”) solutions, and other technologies to customers worldwide across the commercial aerospace and defense sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our sights are set high and our problems are hard, and we believe that diversity in the workplace is what makes us smarter, drives better insights, and will ultimately lift us all to success. We are dedicated to cultivating an equitable and inclusive environment that embraces our differences, and supports and celebrates all of our team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Archer is seeking a motivated and experienced &lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;46&quot;&gt;Cost Accountant&lt;/strong&gt; to join our growing team. In this crucial role, you will leverage your expertise in SAP and cost accounting principles to support our manufacturing costs. As a key contributor, you will play an important role in developing and maintaining cost accounting processes, analyzing financial data, and providing insights to optimize costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Standard Costing:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop, implement, and maintain standard costs in SAP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Cost Updates:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage and establish processes for periodic cost updates and communicate impacts to senior management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Variance Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and manage standard costs for materials, labor, and overhead; track and report variances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with engineering and operations teams to analyze and explain material and labor variances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Data-Driven Insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Analyze historical costs, provide actionable insights, and support data-driven decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,5,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,5,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Financial Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with FP&amp;amp;A business partners to help analyze and explain Budgets vs. Standards vs. Actuals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,6,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,6,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Process Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with cross-functional teams to improve processes, reporting, and automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,7,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,7,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Period Close:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in month-end and quarter-end close processes and provide flux explanations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,8,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,8,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inventory Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare quarterly inventory reserve analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,9,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,9,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Valuation &amp;amp; Reconciliation:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct inventory valuation and reconciliation, including cycle counts and obsolescence reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,10,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,10,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;System Efficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive initiatives for system improvements and efficiencies by participating in UAT and cross-functional projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,11,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,11,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Special Projects:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with cross-functional operational teams on special projects as they pertain to Cost Accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,12,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,12,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Audit Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Finance teams and internal/external auditors as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,13,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,13,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Scalability:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive continuous improvement initiatives to scale cost accounting operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;What You Need&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CMA preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 3–5+ years of cost accounting experience, preferably in complex, multi-plant manufacturing operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with SAP or similar ERP preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;7,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong analytical skills and attention to detail, with the ability to work with complex datasets within Excel and Google Sheets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;7,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Time Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to work in a fast-paced environment and manage multiple priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,5,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;7,5,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Effective communication and presentation skills, with the ability to convey financial concepts to non-financial stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Archer, we aim to attract, retain, and motivate talent with the skills and leadership needed to grow our business. We drive a pay-for-performance culture and reward performance that supports the Company’s strategy. For this position, we are targeting a base pay range of $83,700 - $115,100. Actual compensation offered will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archer is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to job applicants with physical or mental disabilities, and those with sincerely held religious beliefs. Applicants who may require reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should provide their name and contact information to Archer’s People Team at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:people@archer.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;people@archer.com&lt;/a&gt;. Reasonable accommodations will be determined on a case-by-case basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Information collected and processed as part of any job applications you choose to submit is subject to Archer&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://archer.com/legal/personnel-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Certain positions may be eligible for visa sponsorship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Archer is proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer committed to diversity and inclusivity in the workplace. All aspects of employment are decided on the basis of merit, qualifications, and business needs. We do not discriminate based upon race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, gender identity or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Archer Aviation does not engage with external recruiting agencies/individual recruiters with whom it does not have a prior written agreement. Archer reserves the right to make use of any unsolicited resumes that it receives and bears no responsibility for payment of any fees asserted from the use of unsolicited resumes. If you are a recruiting agency or individual recruiter wishing to do business with Archer, please reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:People@archer.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;People@archer.com&lt;/a&gt;. All employment processes are managed by the Archer People Team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Silicon Valley, California, Archer is a leader in the next-gen aerospace sector building an end-to-end advanced air mobility platform that delivers air taxis, unmanned aircraft systems (“UAS”), aviation-related physical artificial intelligence (“AI”) solutions, and other technologies to customers worldwide across the commercial aerospace and defense sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our sights are set high and our problems are hard, and we believe that diversity in the workplace is what makes us smarter, drives better insights, and will ultimately lift us all to success. We are dedicated to cultivating an equitable and inclusive environment that embraces our differences, and supports and celebrates all of our team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;651&quot; data-end=&quot;670&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Archer is best known for Midnight, our electric aircraft. This role isn&#39;t on that program. The AI Products Org builds consumer software for the general aviation industry. There&#39;s a lot we&#39;re not ready to talk about publicly yet, so this posting stays vague on purpose. What we can say: the products are real, they ship, and people use them every day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;As the Deployment Operations Coordinator, you&#39;ll identify, research, and secure host locations near airports for Vantage receiver installations. You&#39;ll be the first point of contact with prospective host businesses — researching candidate sites, cold-calling and emailing property owners and operators, and negotiating hosting agreements — then handing off clean, well-documented sites to the Deployment Engineering team for installation. You&#39;ll also assist with the backend administrative work that keeps the pipeline moving: tracking outreach, processing agreements and paperwork, and coordinating scheduling between hosts and the field team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This role involves equal parts research, phone/email outreach, and the follow-through to keep every site moving from first contact to signed agreement to install-ready.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Research &amp;amp; Outreach:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify candidate businesses near target airports suitable for hosting Vantage receivers (rooftop access, line-of-sight, power availability, etc.)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build and maintain a pipeline of prospective host sites, researching ownership, decision-makers, and site suitability before outreach&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Cold-call and email property/business owners to pitch hosting the equipment, answer questions, and move interested parties toward an agreement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Track outreach activity, responses, and pipeline status in a CRM or tracking system&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Site Agreements &amp;amp; Backend Operations:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Draft, send, and track hosting agreements and related paperwork through signature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Maintain accurate records for each site: contact info, agreement status, site specs, and any special access/logistics notes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordinate scheduling and handoff of signed, install-ready sites to the Deployment Engineering team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Support general program administration — reporting on pipeline metrics, maintaining site databases, and flagging bottlenecks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordination:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Act as liaison between host businesses and Archer&#39;s field team before and after install (initial site walk questions, access coordination, follow-up)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Communicate professionally and persistently with businesses that may be unfamiliar with the technology or hesitant to host equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;About The Team:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AI Products is a roughly 100-person software org inside a company of aerospace engineers, and we expect to grow substantially over the next year. You get the resources and momentum of a real org, but the products themselves are early. If you want to hear more about what we&#39;re building before you apply, you can&#39;t. Apply, and we&#39;ll tell you plenty.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;At Archer we aim to attract, retain, and motivate talent that possess the skills and leadership necessary to grow our business. We drive a pay-for-performance culture and reward performance that supports the Company’s business strategy. For this position we are targeting a &lt;strong&gt;hourly rate of $35 an hour&lt;/strong&gt;. Actual compensation offered will be determined by factors such as job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Archer is committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to job applicants with physical or mental disabilities, and those with sincerely held religious beliefs. Applicants who may require reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should provide their name and contact information to Archer’s People Team at people@archer.com. Reasonable accommodations will be determined on a case-by-case basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Information collected and processed as part of any job applications you choose to submit is subject to Archer&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://archer.com/legal/personnel-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Certain positions may be eligible for visa sponsorship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Archer is proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer committed to diversity and inclusivity in the workplace. All aspects of employment are decided on the basis of merit, qualifications, and business needs. We do not discriminate based upon race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, gender identity or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
