&lt;p&gt;The Total Rewards team partners across Archer to design and execute competitive, compliant compensation, benefits, and equity programs that attract, retain, and motivate world-class talent building the future of flight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Equity Manager, you will own the day-to-day operation and strategic administration of Archer’s global equity compensation programs—ensuring accuracy, compliance, SOX controls, and employee engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Plan Administration:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage grant approvals, vesting, releases, exercises, terminations, participant mobility tracking, and year-end tax reporting (IRC 6039) in compliance with plan terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional &amp;amp; Vendor Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Legal, Finance, Payroll, Tax, and Accounting on Board materials, ASC 718 stock-based compensation, quarterly reconciliations, SOX compliance/audits, and equity platform/HRIS integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Mobility:&lt;/strong&gt; Support Section 16 filings, trading windows&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Education &amp;amp; Advisory:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary equity expert, creating clear communications and running educational sessions (onboarding, vesting, tax guidance) to make equity accessible to all employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; Program Modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Model equity usage, burn rate, dilution, and overhang to inform leadership decisions and improve program design as Archer scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 8+ years of end-to-end stock plan administration experience across public (and ideally high-growth private) environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Platform Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with equity management platforms (e.g., Fidelity, Carta, Shareworks, E*TRADE Equity Edge) and HRIS/payroll integrations (e.g., Workday). Advanced Excel skills required; Modern tooling is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Accounting Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid understanding of ASC 718, SOX controls, Section 1, participant mobility/taxation, and US/global equity structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional attention to detail, discreet handling of confidential/material nonpublic information, and ability to explain complex equity concepts clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fidelity Platform experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified Equity Professional (CEP) designation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth aerospace, deep-tech, or defense sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with global equity programs (specifically EMEA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record implementing equity platforms or automating administration workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
