&lt;p&gt;This is a builder&#39;s role and a player/coach role. You are not only managing a program, you are doing the job alongside your team, personally leading protective details and setting the standard by example. You may come from executive protection directly, or from a related operational background such as special operations, the military, or law enforcement. What matters most is that you can demonstrate the ability to build something from the ground up and that you bring credible, hands-on protective or operational experience. We are looking for a protector who can write the protocols, stand up the details, earn the trust of principals, and still operate in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
