&lt;li&gt;Support litigation matters from intake through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support e-discovery from preservation through production, including advising and assisting with preservation, collection, and production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with investigations to support litigation matters, including working with teams across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help manage and analyze legal spend across the docket, including assisting with budgets, forecasts, and invoice review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with litigation-related scheduling and coordination, including witness interviews, and tracking deadlines across our docket.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help track litigation analytics and trends, including docket and matter reporting, discovery data volumes and trends, and spend analytics to help inform strategy, resources needs, and areas for efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, test, and implement AI-enabled workflows to streamline litigation tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and document repeatable processes, playbooks, and templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of litigation paralegal experience at a law firm or in-house legal department&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a paralegal, including complex e-discovery and experience supporting multiple types of litigation, such as patent litigation, general litigation, employment litigation, and investigations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills and the ability to review and organize numerous documents in complex legal matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills with attention to detail and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to exercise good judgment in the face of ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
