&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our sights are set high and our problems are hard, and we believe that diversity in the workplace is what makes us smarter, drives better insights, and will ultimately lift us all to success. We are dedicated to cultivating an equitable and inclusive environment that embraces our differences, and supports and celebrates all of our team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of design and mechanical system engineers to design and develop high-performance, flight-critical electromechanical actuation systems from concept through production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own overall actuator mechanical design and integration of motors, geartrains, rolling-element screws, bearings, brakes, housings, sensors, and electronics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform trade studies to optimize system architecture and mass while meeting performance and fault-tolerance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and review CAD models, drawings, and engineering specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop actuator-system and detailed component specifications and requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain system-level models to validate actuator performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as single point focal for custom actuation development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work side-by-side with program manager to development and maintain milestone and schedule strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong relationships and work seamlessly with internal functional groups for custom motor, controller, and thermal designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with peer design owners including actuator controller, flight controls, GNC, power systems, airframe, and software to deliver an optimized integrated system for the aircraft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional project teams, coordinating with manufacturing, quality, sourcing, and test engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design reviews and provide technical expertise for key decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example through hands-on problem solving, engineering rigor, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate best practices in documentation, testing, and design validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and oversee junior engineers, fostering professional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with systems, safety, and reliability teams to inform DFMEA and ensure requirements are fully validated and understood&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and oversee technical performance of partnerships and suppliers for varied levels of subassemblies and critical components&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering (or related field)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in actuated mechanism or electromechanical system design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills at any level within the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to take ownership of complex engineering problems through completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated initiative in seeking out critical information and driving technical closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the majority of the following areas:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GD&amp;amp;T for mechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kinematic analysis and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for 14 CFR Part 23 systems compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structural analysis using hand calculations and finite-element methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Materials selection, including alloys, heat treatments, allowables, and surface finishes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Siemens NX CAD and Simcenter or ANSYS FEA tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rolling element bearing selection and sizing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involute gear tooth design and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ball and/or lead screw design and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structural analysis (static, modal, buckling, and fatigue)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PDM systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project or program management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in MATLAB, Python, Mathcad, and/or LabVIEW&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in a machine shop or with mechanical assembly (professional or hobby)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RTCA DO-160, structural, or actuator mechanism testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in aviation, such as pilot training or license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in requirements management tools in the context of aerospace development processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
