&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our sights are set high and our problems are hard, and we believe that diversity in the workplace is what makes us smarter, drives better insights, and will ultimately lift us all to success. We are dedicated to cultivating an equitable and inclusive environment that embraces our differences, and supports and celebrates all of our team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Flight Test Engineer to join our Flight Test and Operational Safety team in support of Halo and Thunder — Archer’s dual-use autonomous VTOL aircraft. This role will plan and execute ground and flight test campaigns, lead safety risk management activities, and mentor junior engineers as we advance Halo and Thunder toward first flight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare development and Company ground and flight test plans supporting Halo and Thunder flight test campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run flight test cards through sim with remote/ground control station operators and autonomy engineers for optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in all aspects of the Flight Test Safety Risk Management process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare test operating limitations and advisories in collaboration with the appropriate engineering disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with engineering, certification, and quality teams to ensure test objectives are clearly defined and achieved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and document test article configuration, maintenance activities, and modifications during Halo and Thunder test campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in safety risk management activities and help maintain compliance with applicable safety standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain flight test instrumentation and data acquisition systems, supporting accurate data collection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s/Master’s Degree in Aerospace Engineering, Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in flight test operations, aerospace testing, or a related technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with safety risk management processes related to flight testing or complex operational testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in configuration management and planning/executing ground and flight tests within certification or military projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading multidisciplinary teams or organizations within a test or development environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional collaboration and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to thrive in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note that this job description is intended to provide a general overview of the position and does not include an exhaustive list of responsibilities and qualifications.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
