&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a multidisciplinary team of engineers specializing in loads analysis, dynamics, aeroelasticity, ASE and rotordynamics for eVTOL aircraft development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership and strategic direction for all loads and dynamics activities from preliminary design through certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical roadmap for loads development processes, ensuring compliance with certification requirements (14 CFR Parts 23, 27, and 35)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the development of static and fatigue loads databases to support airframe, engine, mechanical systems, and propeller design teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional collaboration with aerodynamics, airframe, mass properties, flight dynamics, and propulsion teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the development and validation of comprehensive analysis toolchains for loads, aeroelasticity, and rotordynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage certification activities related to loads means and methods of compliance discussions with the FAA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely delivery of loads data and analyses to internal and external customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop team members&#39; technical capabilities and career growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster innovation in loads analysis methods for advanced eVTOL configurations including tilting mechanisms and variable pitch systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS/PhD in Aerospace Engineering or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of industry experience with 5+ years in technical leadership roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in aircraft loads analysis, aeroelasticity, and structural dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in rotorcraft and/or fixed-wing aircraft development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership experience managing technical teams and complex projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of finite element modeling and structural analysis methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python and/or Matlab scripting for loads analysis automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent technical communication skills with ability to present to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced design environments with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills to coordinate multidisciplinary teams on time-critical projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Archer we aim to attract, retain, and motivate talent that possess the skills and leadership necessary to grow our business. We drive a pay-for-performance culture and reward performance that supports the Company’s business strategy. For this position we are targeting a base pay between $207,000 - $259,000. Actual compensation offered will be determined by factors such as job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
