&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Silicon Valley, California, Archer is a leader in the next-gen aerospace sector building an end-to-end advanced air mobility platform that delivers air taxis, unmanned aircraft systems (“UAS”), aviation-related physical artificial intelligence (“AI”) solutions, and other technologies to customers worldwide across the commercial aerospace and defense sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our sights are set high and our problems are hard, and we believe that diversity in the workplace is what makes us smarter, drives better insights, and will ultimately lift us all to success. We are dedicated to cultivating an equitable and inclusive environment that embraces our differences, and supports and celebrates all of our team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Development Assurance team, in this pivotal role, you will be instrumental in launching our first certified aircraft by architecting the engineering framework that governs how we work. You will define, deploy, and continuously improve the processes and toolchains that enable our teams to develop cutting-edge aircraft systems with the highest standards of quality, safety, and efficiency. As a multi-disciplinary leader, you will bridge the gap between engineering execution and company strategy, ensuring our development lifecycle is fully compliant ARP4754A and other aerospace industry standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the definition, implementation, and continuous improvement of a comprehensive Systems Engineering framework fully compliant with ARP4754A.&amp;nbsp; Ensure that our engineering processes and artifacts not only meet the objectives of ARP4754A, DO-178C, and DO-254 but also generate the clear, traceable evidence required for successful audits and certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and govern the standards, templates, and quality criteria for all key development artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll be a trusted partner and coach to engineering teams, helping them understand the &quot;why&quot; behind the process and integrating their feedback to create a system that works for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with multidisciplinary engineering teams to integrate compliant processes and artifact standards into their daily workflows, providing training and support to ensure practical and consistent application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Product Lifecycle Engineering and Tools teams to configure our engineering toolchain to enforce process compliance, automate traceability, and manage the lifecycle of all certified artifacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS, MS, or PhD in Systems Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ yrs of experience in developing one or more aerospace systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven background in developing and verifying highly integrated aerospace systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with requirements development, configuration, and architecture definition for aircraft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with civil aviation programs utilizing Systems Engineering processes for certification credit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of systems engineering practices and the underlying reasons and purpose behind them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience using one or more requirements management tools (e.g., Polarion, DOORS, Jama).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full understanding of the Systems Engineering standard used in civil aviation and the underlying reasons and purpose for each process and activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience defining, implementing, and providing training for engineering processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulations and standards for transport and general aviation aircraft (14 CFR Part 23/27)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on Type Certification from concept to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
