&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Silicon Valley, California, Archer is a leader in the next-gen aerospace sector building an end-to-end advanced air mobility platform that delivers air taxis, unmanned aircraft systems (“UAS”), aviation-related physical artificial intelligence (“AI”) solutions, and other technologies to customers worldwide across the commercial aerospace and defense sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our sights are set high and our problems are hard, and we believe that diversity in the workplace is what makes us smarter, drives better insights, and will ultimately lift us all to success. We are dedicated to cultivating an equitable and inclusive environment that embraces our differences, and supports and celebrates all of our team members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wire harness routing and installation design using 3D CAD (Siemens NX)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow industry best practices and guidance for the design and installation of the wire harnesses (AC 43.13-1B, AS50881, ASTM F2639).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your knowledge of industry standard components to select the best parts to suit specific design applications and requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position aircraft components, equipment and support structures to provide optimal wire routing with respect to safety, weight and installation easement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide installation instructions and guidance for the assembly and integration of the harnesses and associated subcomponents into the Aircraft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and apply inspection criteria for the manufactured and installed components in accordance with best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use strong configuration and change management skills to track the changes to the components throughout the lifetime of the aircraft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to look for alternative solutions and come up with custom parts to resolve wire routing in tight areas and around moving components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical, Electrical, Aerospace Engineering or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5 years of experience in engineering and design of aircraft wiring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using 3D CAD software and Electrical routing modules/workbenches : Siemens NX and Electrical Routing Package (Preferred), Catia V5 Electrical Workbench&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Wiring CAD software : Mentor Graphics Capital, HarnessXC and Logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience in the processes involved in fabricating, installing, and inspecting harnesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of EWIS concepts, certification and experience with FAA AC 25.1701&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Siemens NX Formboard and bridging with Mentor Graphics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3D printing and/or injection molding experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best practices for lightning, HIRF and grounding on composite aircraft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
